explanation:
Anton Von Leeuwenhoek first observed and described live microorganisms, such as bacteria and protozoa,
              using a simple microscope in the 1670s (NCERT, Chapter 8, page 125). Robert Brown discovered the nucleus,
              Schleiden contributed to cell theory, and Virchow proposed that cells arise from pre-existing cells.

Carrier proteins facilitate active transport by moving molecules against their concentration gradient
              using energy (NCERT, Chapter 8, page 128). Phospholipids form the bilayer, cholesterol maintains fluidity,
              and glycoproteins aid in cell recognition.

